    takeaway: `Task-specific weight updates have low intrinsic rank — LoRA exploits this to fine-tune a 70B model with 0.2% of its parameters. Because the adapter matrices merge directly into the base weights, the deployed model is byte-for-byte identical at inference: zero latency overhead, the only reason to use adapters instead.`,
